16sv|n|See Loon, the bird. ; A frame or machine of wood or other material, in which a weaver forms cloth out of thread; a machine for interweaving yarn or threads into a fabric, as in knitting or lace making. ; That part of an oar which is near the grip or handle and inboard from the rowlock. ; The state of looming; esp., an unnatural and indistinct appearance of elevation or enlargement of anything, as of land or of a ship, seen by one at sea.	n:28y5,104,3~28y5,104,3
